<title>GERMANY: Winter weather seen hardening German crops - Toepfer.</title>
<headline>Winter weather seen hardening German crops - Toepfer.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German winter rapeseed and barley suffered some damage during the recent frost period but the big chill will also have hardened them against pests and diseases later on, grain trader Alfred C Toepfer's monthly report said.</p>
<p>Severe winter conditions in 1995-96 brought some winter kill in some areas but yields in the majority of regions were excellent because the surviving plants were very robust, it noted.</p>
<p>But the trader also said rainfall in December only constituted between 45 and 65 percent of the long-term average for that month.</p>
</text>
